          en: 'To develop a more robust study method, investigate learning techniques based on scientific evidence. Active retrieval (trying to remember information without consulting the source) is proven more efficient than rereading. Spaced repetition (revisiting content at increasing intervals) combats the forgetting curve. Interleaving (alternating between related topics) strengthens conceptual connections. Applying these principles to programming study transforms efficiency measurably. Additionally, maintain a record of what you studied: a repository with notes, implemented examples, and solved problems functions as external memory and learning portfolio simultaneously.',
