          en: 'The choice between courses, college, and self-teaching is not a question of right or wrong — it is a question of fitness to context. The mature professional evaluates their circumstances honestly, identifies their real needs, and chooses the path that maximizes return on available resources. And recognizes that this choice can be revised and complemented over time. Education does not end when the course finishes or when the diploma is delivered. It continues as long as the career continues, and the ability to learn autonomously is the common denominator of all successful professionals, regardless of where they started.',
