          en: 'To go deeper, study time management methodologies like Pomodoro (focused twenty-five-minute sessions with breaks), time blocking (reserving specific calendar blocks for study), and the Pareto principle applied to learning (identifying the twenty percent of concepts that cover eighty percent of practical situations). Experiment with different approaches and maintain records to evaluate which works best for your profile and context.',
